NAME
       socket, bind, listen, accept, connect - BSD sockets

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/socket.h>

       int socket(int domain, int type, int protocol);
       int bind(int s, const struct sockaddr *a, socklen_t len);
       int listen(int s, int backlog);
       int accept(int s, struct sockaddr *a, socklen_t *len);
       int connect(int s, const struct sockaddr *a, socklen_t len);
       ssize_t send(int s, const void *buf, size_t n, int flags);
       ssize_t recv(int s, void *buf, size_t n, int flags);

DESCRIPTION
       The usual socket calls. AF_INET, AF_INET6 and AF_UNIX are
       supported, with SOCK_STREAM and SOCK_DGRAM.

       A socket put into non-blocking mode makes connect return at once
       and finish in the background, which is what lets nmap(1) scan a
       wide range quickly.

RETURN VALUE
       socket and accept return a descriptor; the rest return 0. All
       return -1 with errno set on failure.

ERRORS
       EAFNOSUPPORT   the domain is not supported
       EADDRINUSE     the address is already bound
       ECONNREFUSED   nothing is listening
       EAGAIN         a non-blocking operation is still in progress

SEE ALSO
       sendto(2), poll(2), nc(1)
